{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1030 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "e63c54b8afe873621a15ced58d694263f8ec7cf7d87a4962ae0d06d24c469ab1" :edb/db-before-t 1029 :edb/db-after-t 1030 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534342 50 #inst "2026-10-11T19:24:45.184Z" 13194139534342 17592186045417 true] [17592186127321 1078 #edb/ref 17592186127325 13194139534342 17592186045417 true] [17592186129130 1038 #edb/ref 17592186419683 13194139534342 17592186045417 true] [17592186129131 1038 #edb/ref 17592186419684 13194139534342 17592186045417 true] [17592186129155 1038 #edb/ref 17592186419685 13194139534342 17592186045417 true] [17592186129213 1038 #edb/ref 17592186419686 13194139534342 17592186045417 true] [17592186129640 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534342 17592186045417 true] [17592186129640 1071 "Let $[T]_{B}$ and $[T]_{C}$ be the matrices of a linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$, respectively. If $P_{B → C}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from basis $B$ to basis $C$, which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $[T]_{C} = P_{B → C} \\cdot [T]_{B} \\cdot P_{B → C}^{-1}$\n2. $[T]_{C} = P_{B → C}^{-1} \\cdot [T]_{B} \\cdot P_{B → C}$\n3. $[T]_{B} = P_{B → C}^{-1} \\cdot [T]_{C} \\cdot P_{B → C}$" 13194139534342 17592186045417 false] [17592186129640 1071 "Let $[T]_{B}$ and $[T]_{C}$ be the matrices of a linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C,$ respectively. If ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from basis $B$ to basis $C,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}$\n- $[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}$\n- $[T]_{B}={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}$" 13194139534342 17592186045417 true] [17592186129640 1074 "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/1b/1b81504d6fdcabee0e1f586fef3dd2af5a57a8411ba4d22429e00e09b171a4d1.png)\n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$\n\nSolving this equation for $[T]_{B},$ we obtain the alternative formulation\n\n$$\n[T]_{B}={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139534342 17592186045417 true] [17592186419658 1043 #edb/ref 17592186419687 13194139534342 17592186045417 true] [17592186419658 1043 #edb/ref 17592186419688 13194139534342 17592186045417 true] [17592186419658 1043 #edb/ref 17592186419689 13194139534342 17592186045417 true] [17592186419658 1043 #edb/ref 17592186419690 13194139534342 17592186045417 true] [17592186419658 1043 #edb/ref 17592186419691 13194139534342 17592186045417 true] [17592186419658 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534342 17592186045417 true] [17592186419658 1045 "Connections Between Matrix Representations of a Linear Transformation" 13194139534342 17592186045417 true] [17592186419658 1046 #edb/ref 17592186419688 13194139534342 17592186045417 true] [17592186419658 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046673 13194139534342 17592186045417 true] [17592186419658 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050324 13194139534342 17592186045417 true] [17592186419658 1053 #uuid "a3e8a2c7-af14-540f-a7b1-76dc269d676b" 13194139534342 17592186045417 true] [17592186419659 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]" 13194139534342 17592186045417 true] [17592186419659 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534342 17592186045417 true] [17592186419659 1083 #uuid "094350f2-e017-53e0-b0e9-5075268dbe4d" 13194139534342 17592186045417 true] [17592186419660 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]" 13194139534342 17592186045417 true] [17592186419660 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534342 17592186045417 true] [17592186419660 1083